# In "Simpler authentication for small scale JupyterHubs", the thank-you
# link on "Berkeley Institute for Data Science" carries the whole
# acknowledgement sentence as its URL ("http://I am grateful to the
# Berkeley Institute for Data Science & NumFocus for jointly sponsoring
# my Outreachy internship"), authored that way on Medium. Hugo's URL
# parser rejects it. Point it at BIDS. (The href lives in the page's
# embedded editor state; replacing an href value is safe -- markup
# offsets index the paragraph text, which is untouched.)
file: 999534c77a09/page.html
old-regex: http:(\\u002F\\u002F|//)I am grateful[^"]*
new: https://bids.berkeley.edu/
